@startuml managed_agents_resource_model
title Anthropic Managed Agents Public Resource Model
top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 35
skinparam ArrowColor #53657D
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #53657D
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #F7F9FC

' Source evidence:
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/agent-setup
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/sessions
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/environments
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/memory
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/vaults
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/multiagent-orchestration
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/scheduled-deployments
' Observed behavior: an agent is versioned, an environment is not versioned, and each session receives an isolated sandbox.
' Observed behavior: vaults and memory stores are referenced by a session instead of being embedded in the reusable agent.
' Design reason: the layout centers the session and records only public relationships without inferring internal implementation.

package "Reusable configuration" #EAF2FF {
  rectangle "Skill\ncustom or Anthropic" as Skill
  rectangle "Agent\nversioned" as Agent
  rectangle "Environment\nunversioned" as Environment
  Skill -[hidden]down- Agent
  Agent -[hidden]right- Environment
}
package "Session resources" #E9F7EF {
  rectangle "Session\nruntime state machine" as Session
  rectangle "Agent snapshot\nid, version, overrides" as Snapshot
  rectangle "Sandbox\nisolated per Session" as Sandbox
  rectangle "Session thread\nisolated conversation" as Thread
  rectangle "Event stream\npersisted complete events" as Event
  Snapshot -[hidden]right- Sandbox
}
package "Workspace services" #FFF4E6 {
  rectangle "Vault\ncredentials" as Vault
  rectangle "Memory Store\ntext documents" as MemoryStore
  rectangle "Deployment\nschedule + Session config" as Deployment
  rectangle "Deployment run\nsession_id or error" as DeploymentRun
  Vault -[hidden]down- MemoryStore
  MemoryStore -[hidden]down- Deployment
}
Skill --> Agent : skills
Agent --> Session : resolve version
Environment --> Session : environment_id
Vault -[norank]-> Session : vault_ids
MemoryStore -[norank]-> Session : resources
Session *--> Snapshot : freezes
Session *--> Sandbox : provisions
Session *--> "1..*" Thread
Thread *--> "0..*" Event
Deployment -[norank]-> Agent : Agent config
Deployment -[norank]-> Environment : Environment config
Deployment *--> "0..*" DeploymentRun
Deployment -[norank]-> Session : schedules
legend bottom left
Public resource relationships, not internal tables or services.
Session: idle / running / rescheduling / terminated.
Vault: at most 20 credentials. Exact fields and event types are in the document.
endlegend

@enduml

@startuml session_agent_creation_sequence
' Source evidence:
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/sessions
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/beta/sessions/create
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/environments
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/tools
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/mcp-connector
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/skills
' Observed behavior: a session stores a resolved agent snapshot, provisions an isolated sandbox, starts idle when initial_events is omitted or empty, and begins work after a user event is accepted.
' Logical inference: component boundaries and the exact preparation order below are explanatory architecture, not claims about Anthropic internal implementation.
' Design reason: separate immutable agent version resolution from session-local overrides and runtime resource preparation so the resulting session is traceable.
title Managed Agents: Create, Then Start Work
' Public contract checked 2026-09-14: sessions, create Session, and events-and-streaming.
' Observed update: a non-empty initial_events list starts the Session as running.
' Logical inference: API self-actions summarize public effects, not internal service order.
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
}

actor Client
boundary "Managed Agents\nSession API" as API
participant "Claude Model" as Model

== 1. Resolve the Session ==
Client -> API : Create Session\nAgent and Environment references
API -> API : Resolve latest or pinned Agent version
API -> API : Apply complete-field overrides
break Invalid effective configuration
  API --> Client : Validation error; no Session
end
API -> API : Prepare isolated sandbox and resources
API -> API : Capture resolved Agent configuration

== 2. Select the start boundary ==
alt initial_events omitted or empty
  API --> Client : Session: idle
  ... Client starts a task later ...
  Client -> API : Send user.message
  API --> Client : Accepted event
else Non-empty initial_events
  API -> API : Validate and persist initial events
  API --> Client : Session: running
end

== 3. Observe work ==
API -> Model : Run with resolved context and tools
Model --> API : Message or tool request
Client -> API : Open event stream
API -->> Client : Session and Agent events

legend bottom left
Beta public contract; internal preparation order is not published.
Session overrides do not create a new Agent version.
initial_events: user.message / user.define_outcome only; at most 50.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml managed_agent_configuration_model
title Anthropic Managed Agent Public Configuration Model
top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam ArrowColor #53657D
skinparam ClassBorderColor #53657D
