@startuml managed_agents_tool_execution_model
' Source evidence:
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/tools
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/mcp-connector
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/events-and-streaming
' - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/vaults
' Observed behavior: built-in tools run in the session sandbox, MCP tools run on the declared remote server, and custom tools run in the client application.
' Observed behavior: always_ask pauses the session for user.tool_confirmation; custom calls pause for user.custom_tool_result.
' Design reason: the sequence separates declaration from runtime ownership and does not imply a shared executable format.
title Managed Agents: Who Executes Each Tool?
' Public contract checked 2026-09-14: tools and events-and-streaming.
' Design reason: each branch exposes only the public API and the actual executor.
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
}

actor "Client application" as Client
boundary "Managed Agents API" as API
participant "Session sandbox" as Sandbox
participant "Remote MCP server" as MCP

Client -> API : Send user.message
API --> Client : Accepted event

== Server-executed tools ==
alt Built-in tool selected
  API -->> Client : agent.tool_use
  opt permission_policy = always_ask
    API -->> Client : Idle: requires_action
    Client -> API : user.tool_confirmation
  end
  alt Allowed
    API -> Sandbox : Execute built-in tool
    Sandbox --> API : Tool result
  else Denied
    API -> API : Continue without executing the tool
  end
else MCP tool selected
  API -->> Client : agent.mcp_tool_use
  opt permission_policy = always_ask
    API -->> Client : Idle: requires_action
    Client -> API : user.tool_confirmation
  end
  alt Allowed
    API -> MCP : tools/call\nSession Vault credential
    MCP --> API : Tool result
  else Denied
    API -> API : Continue without executing the tool
  end
end

== Application-executed tool ==
API -->> Client : agent.custom_tool_use\nIdle: requires_action
Client -> Client : Execute application code
Client -> API : user.custom_tool_result
API -> API : Resume when blocking calls resolve
API -->> Client : agent.message and Session status

legend bottom left
Illustrative tool paths; not a requirement to call all three tool types.
Custom tools are controlled by the application, outside permission_policy.
Credentials belong to Session bindings, not reusable Agent definitions.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml managed_agents_session_history_recovery
' Official source evidence accessed 2026-08-16:
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/beta/sessions/events/list
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/typescript/beta/sessions/threads/events/list
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/events-and-streaming
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/session-operations
' Observed behavior: GET Session retrieves the session resource, while persisted conversation
' history is listed from GET /v1/sessions/{session_id}/events.
' Observed behavior: event_start and event_delta are best-effort stream previews; they are never
' persisted or replayed, and the buffered agent.message is the authoritative record.
' Observed behavior: multiagent child histories and live previews are thread-scoped.
' Design reason: the client rebuilds display state from persisted events, opens the live stream,
' and replaces temporary previews when the authoritative buffered event arrives.
title Managed Agents: Restore History and Reconcile Preview
' Public contract checked 2026-09-14: events-and-streaming.
' Design reason: one API participant represents public endpoints; the reducer is a client responsibility.
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
}

actor User
boundary "Client UI" as Client
control "Conversation\nprojection" as View
boundary "Managed Agents\nPublic APIs" as API

== 1. Restore authoritative history ==
User -> Client : Open Session
Client -> API : Retrieve Session
API --> Client : Resource and current status
loop Until next_page is null
  Client -> API : List events: order=asc, page
  API --> Client : Persisted event page
  Client -> View : Apply complete events in order
end
opt Multiagent Session
  Client -> API : List Threads and visible Thread history
  API --> Client : Thread resources and event pages
  Client -> View : Build each Thread timeline
end
View --> Client : Restored display

== 2. Reconcile live preview ==
Client -> API : Open stream with agent.message deltas
API -->> Client : event_start / event_delta
Client -> View : Accumulate by event ID and content index
API -->> Client : Complete agent.message
Client -> View : Replace matching preview
View --> Client : Authoritative message

== 3. Recover after disconnect ==
... Connection lost ...
Client -> API : Reopen event stream
Client -> API : Query persisted history again
API --> Client : Complete events missed offline
Client -> View : Deduplicate IDs and reconcile
View --> Client : Recovered display

legend bottom left
Preview is best-effort, never persisted or replayed.
The complete event is authoritative; child previews stay Thread-scoped.
Endpoint paths and paging fields are listed in the accompanying document.
endlegend
